{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791726018,"nonce":"7bRt8qlO6Hz0ftMO7uOK1BnFQJc=","title":"CI's Vite HMR test misses saves on Node 24, and blinc() overrides watch: null","message":"The sdk (24) job failed intermittently (aeee89b, b06da41, 2e628aa): the HMR test's saved edit was never seen, with zero updates after 8 s. Diagnostics showed the watcher watching the fixture directory but reporting no events. Moving from polling to inotify on Linux did not cure it, and it never reproduced locally, on the NUC, or on Node 24.21.\n\nThe test is about what HMR does with a change, so it now runs Vite with watch: null and reports each save to Vite's watcher itself. That exposed a plugin bug: blinc() returned server.watch.ignored, and Vite's config merge turned the app's watch: null back into a real watcher. blinc() now adds its ignore list only when watching is on, and the test asserts the watcher stays the no-op one. With the old plugin the assertion fails.","files":null}]}